/-!
# Colle, arXiv:1909.08195v4, Proposition 2.10

## The source, quoted verbatim

Colle states the ambiguity notion in §2.3 ("Periodicity"), just before the
proposition.  Verbatim from the arXiv v4 LaTeX source (`OnNonexdirNC.tex`,
lines 338-347), with `\sob{X}` rendered as `|_X`:

> Let `ℓ ⊂ ℝ²` be an oriented line through the origin and suppose that
> `𝒮 ⊂ ℤ²` is a non-empty, finite, convex set.  For each
> `γ ∈ pat(𝒮 \ ℓ_𝒮, η)`, we define
> `N_𝒮(ℓ,γ) := |{γ' ∈ pat(𝒮,η) : γ'|_{𝒮 \ ℓ_𝒮} = γ}|`.
> Notice that `N_𝒮(ℓ,γ) = 1` means that `γ'|_{𝒮\ℓ_𝒮} = γ = γ''|_{𝒮\ℓ_𝒮}`
> implies `γ' = γ''` for any `γ',γ'' ∈ pat(𝒮,η)`.  Let `ℓ ⊂ ℝ²` be a
> rational oriented line through the origin.  A configuration `x ∈ X_η` is
> said to be *`(ℓ,𝒮)`-ambiguous* if,
> `∀ 𝒮 \ ℓ_𝒮-pattern γ = (T^{t v_ℓ} x)|_{𝒮 \ ℓ_𝒮}, t ∈ ℤ, one has N_𝒮(ℓ,γ) > 1`,
> where `v_ℓ ∈ ℓ ∩ ℤ²` denotes the non-zero vector parallel to `ℓ` of
> minimum norm.

And the proposition itself (same file, lines 356-358):

> **Proposition 2.10 (Cyr and Kra [van]).**
> Let `η ∈ 𝒜^{ℤ²}` be a configuration and suppose `ℓ ∈ ONED(η)`.  If there
> exists an `η`-generating set `𝒮 ⊂ ℤ²`, with `|𝒮 ∩ ℓ_𝒮| ≤ |𝒮 ∩ -ℓ_𝒮|`,
> such that `P_η(𝒮) - P_η(𝒮 \ ℓ_𝒮) ≤ |𝒮 ∩ ℓ_𝒮| - 1`, then, for any
> `(ℓ,𝒮)`-ambiguous configuration `x ∈ X_η`, the restriction of `x` to the
> half plane `ℋ(-ℓ_𝒮)` is periodic with period parallel to `ℓ`.

Supporting definitions quoted from the same source:

* Definition 2.1 (line 260-262): "The *support line of `𝒮`* determined by
  `ℓ`, denoted by `ℓ_𝒮`, is defined as the oriented line `ℓ'` parallel to
  `ℓ` such that `𝒮 ⊂ ℋ(ℓ')` and `ℓ' ∩ 𝒮 ≠ ∅`."
* Half plane (line 132): "`ℋ(ℓ) := {g ∈ ℤ² : ⟨g,(-u₂,u₁)⟩ ≥ 0}`, where
  `(u₁,u₂) ∈ ℝ²` is a non-zero vector parallel to `ℓ`."
* Definition 2.2 (line 278-280): "A point `g ∈ 𝒮` is said to be
  *`η`-generated by `𝒮`* if `P_η(𝒮) = P_η(𝒮 \ {g})`.  A non-empty, finite,
  convex subset of `ℤ²` for which each vertex is `η`-generated is called an
  *`η`-generating set*."
* Restricted periodicity, Definition 2.11 (line 364-366): "`η|_𝒰` is
  *periodic* if there exists `h ∈ (ℤ²)*` such that `η_{g+h} = η_g` for all
  `g ∈ 𝒰 ∩ (𝒰 - h)`."

**Colle gives no proof.**  Line 354 reads: "The next result is a summary of
two results of [van], namely, Lemma 2.24 and a piece of the proof of
Proposition 4.8."  `[van]` is Cyr-Kra, *Nonexpansive `ℤ²`-Subdynamics and
Nivat's Conjecture*, Trans. AMS 367 (2015) 6487-6537, arXiv:1208.4090.  So
the actual mathematical content is:

* **Cyr-Kra Lemma 2.24** (arXiv:1208.4090, `\label{ambiguousperiod}`): the
  ambiguity along `ℓ` plus the counting bound forces the *row sequence* of
  `x` transverse to `ℓ` to have one-dimensional block complexity
  `P_g(h) ≤ h` for `h := |𝒮 ∩ ℓ_𝒮| - 1`, so Morse-Hedlund makes it periodic
  of period at most `h`.  This gives periodicity on a **strip** of bounded
  width along `ℓ_𝒮`, not yet on the half plane.
* **Cyr-Kra Proposition 4.8**, subsection "Periodicity of `f|_{B_K}` for
  `K < 0`": a downward induction on strips `B_K` which upgrades the strip
  to the whole half plane `ℤ² \ H = ℋ(-ℓ_𝒮)`, with period at most `2h`.
  Its two base claims are (i) the non-unique-extension case (pigeonhole on
  the at most `2h` `𝒮`-colourings whose restriction is ambiguous, plus the
  minimal-vertical-period argument) and (ii) the unique-extension case (a
  gluing construction producing a second element of `X_𝒮(η)`).

## Conventions used here

An oriented line `ℓ` through the origin is recorded by a primitive
direction `v : ℤ × ℤ` together with a real normal `w : ℝ × ℝ` with
`inner2 w v = 0`, oriented so that Colle's `ℋ(ℓ')` for the line `ℓ'` at
level `c` is `{z | c ≤ inner2 w z}`.  Consequently, for a finite `S`:

* `ℓ_S` is the level `c = min_{z ∈ S} inner2 w z`;
* `S ∩ ℓ_S` is `S.filter (fun z => inner2 w z = c)`;
* `S \ ℓ_S` is `S.filter (fun z => c < inner2 w z)`;
* `S ∩ (-ℓ)_S` is `S.filter (fun z => inner2 w z = c')` with
  `c' = max_{z ∈ S} inner2 w z`;
* `ℋ(-ℓ_S)` is `{z | inner2 w z ≤ c}`.

Since `inner2 w v = 0`, the half plane `ℋ(-ℓ_S)` is invariant under
translation by any multiple of `v`, so Colle's restricted periodicity
`η_{g+h} = η_g for g ∈ 𝒰 ∩ (𝒰 - h)` becomes simply
`∀ z, inner2 w z ≤ c → x (z + u) = x z`.

## What is proved here

* `AmbiguousAlong` — Colle's `(ℓ,𝒮)`-ambiguity, spelled out without
  subtypes.  Source: the quoted definition above.
* `exists_ambiguous_pattern_of_ambiguousAlong` — the bridge from
  `AmbiguousAlong` to this repository's `Nivat.Colle.ambiguous_patterns`.
  Proved.
* `two_le_card_face_of_oneSidedNonexpansive` — if `S` is an `η`-generating
  set and the face `S ∩ ℓ_S` is a single point, then `ℓ ∉ ONED(η)`.  This is
  Colle Lemma 2.3, and it is what makes `h := |S ∩ ℓ_S| - 1` positive in
  Proposition 2.10.  Proved, from `eq_of_halfPlane_of_generatesAt`
  (Lemma 2.3 machinery, already in `GeneratedHalfPlane.lean`) and
  `latticeConvex_filter_inner2_lt` (already in `LowComplexityWindow.lean`).
* `exists_row_period_of_ambiguousAlong` — **the core of Cyr-Kra Lemma 2.24**,
  fully proved: ambiguity along `v` + the counting bound
  `P η S - P η Q ≤ h` + a finite set `B` with `B + j•v ⊆ Q` for `j < h`
  force a period `q•v` with `0 < q` on the union of the lines through `B`.
  Ingredients: `ncard_ambiguous_patterns_le_sub`
  (`AmbiguousCounting.lean`, already proved) and
  `Nivat.periodic_of_subwords_le` (`Nivat/MorseHedlund.lean`, already
  proved).
* `exists_rowBase_of_latticeConvex` — **Cyr-Kra's height lemma plus row
  structure**, fully proved (unconditionally).  The height lemma proper is
  already in this repository as `Nivat.card_row_ge_of_extreme`
  (`Nivat/Chord.lean`); what is added here is (a) the translation between
  Colle's *real* linear form `inner2 w` and the *integral* form `det v ·`
  (`exists_ratio_of_inner2_eq_zero`: they differ by a non-zero real factor
  `μ`, so they have the same level sets), and (b) the fact that each row of
  a lattice-convex set is a contiguous run of lattice points along `v`
  (`mem_row_of_between`, two-point convexity).  The base set `B` is
  Cyr-Kra's family of `x_ℓ`, the bottom-most point of each row.
* `exists_strip_period_of_ambiguousAlong` — the two previous items
  combined: a period `q•v` on the whole strip `c < inner2 w z ≤ c'`.
  Proved, unconditionally.

## Hypothesis provenance

Every hypothesis of `exists_row_period_of_ambiguousAlong` is supplied
downstream by already-proved material:

* `hξ : (Set.range ξ).Finite` — the standing finite-range assumption of §8
  of the host paper; `patterns_finite_of_range_finite` is proved.
* `hx : x ∈ orbitClosure ξ` — `x ∈ X_η` in Colle's notation.
* `hQS : Q ⊆ S` — `S \ ℓ_S ⊆ S`.
* `hcount : P ξ S - P ξ Q ≤ h` — literally Colle's complexity hypothesis;
  `exists_generatingSet_with_boundary_deficit` (Colle Lemma 2.4,
  `LowComplexityGenerating.lean`) produces a generating set satisfying it.
* `hh : 0 < h` — from `two_le_card_face_of_oneSidedNonexpansive`, proved
  below, i.e. from `ℓ ∈ ONED(η)` and `S` generating.
* `hrow` — the *only* geometric input, supplied by
  `exists_rowBase_of_latticeConvex` below (Cyr-Kra's height lemma), which
  is now **proved unconditionally**.  It is a statement about
  lattice-convex polygons alone; it mentions neither `η` nor complexity,
  so it is not a disguised form of the conclusion.

## Remaining `sorry`s

None.  `colle_prop_2_10` and the downward induction of **Cyr-Kra Proposition
4.8** it rests on (`cyrKra_downward_induction`, §4.2.1-§4.2.3 of
arXiv:1208.4090) are both proved unconditionally, as is everything else in
this file, including the geometric input `exists_rowBase_of_latticeConvex`
and the strip periodicity `exists_strip_period_of_ambiguousAlong`.

The route taken for §4.2.1 departs from Cyr-Kra's: instead of Corollary 2.25
(borders / subextensions / `m`-interiors, still absent from this repository) it
extracts a *bounded determinacy window* `k ≤ h` from the ambiguity
(`exists_row_determinacy_of_ambiguousAlong`, a two-sided Morse-Hedlund
argument), and obtains the candidate shift from an independent pigeonhole over
`S`-patterns, bounded by `P η(𝒮)`.  See the note attached to
`cyrKra_downward_induction` for the full accounting.  Note that the strip
produced by `exists_strip_period_of_ambiguousAlong` sits at levels
`c < inner2 w z ≤ c'` whereas the target half-plane is `inner2 w z ≤ c`: the
two regions are disjoint, so no repackaging of the strip result can reach the
goal; the downward propagation *is* the content of §4.2.3.

Nothing in this file weakens or strengthens Colle's statement except that
`colle_prop_2_10` carries the one-sided nonexpansiveness hypothesis
`honed` written out explicitly (Colle's `ℓ ∈ ONED(η)`) rather than through
`Nivat.ONED`, in order to keep this file free of the axioms declared in
`Nivat/Section8/External.lean`.

